			<div class="content" id="post-content-1452791">
									

<p>I'm withholding my upvote until it's cleaned up a bit. As mentioned above, there's some spelling issues, and the containment procedures could use some work. A Foundation operative was [DATA EXPUNGED]'d for not paying a $16 dollar receipt, so I imagine it would be more logical to require researchers to at least carry a twenty around.</p>
<p>Also, there's some issues with clinical tone. &quot;The van waited as if it were thinking&quot; could probably be written differently. And is there a reason D-Class personnel aren't being used for the experimentation, rather than putting Foundation staff at risk? I realize that &quot;getting an ice cream cone&quot; is probably far too nice an outcome for a D-Class in this universe, but that seems like basic procedure.</p>
<p>And yes, I realize I'm nitpicking a magical, sapient ice cream truck.</p>

